e a dramatic shift  in ct to the right where the samples are  coming up much later  and this is due to these inhibitor  samples and this clearly is going to  decrease your sensitivity when doing a  pcr you won't detect positive samples if  you do not remove your inhibitors ahead  of time  um and so we looked at this we looked to  see how critical it is for  wastewater samples to use irt so irt is  kyogen's proprietary inhibitor removal  technology it is present in any kit that  has power in its name so the all-prep  power viral the rna-z power water the r  and e-z power microbiome for example  those all contain this irt  now the chi amp viral rna mini kit is  standardly used for stars cov2  detection of extraction and analysis in  swab samples for example but it's not  designed to deal with fecal material or  sewage samples and here when we compare  it we see that as well using  um  different concentration methods whether  we spun down and processed a pellet or  did ultra  filtration or did electronegative  filtration on a mix cellulose ester  membrane  we see a significant background shift in  cts when we prep those materials with  the ky amp viral rna mini kit and we see  much better consistent detection using  either the all prep power viral or the  rnez power water kit and this is an  indication that there are potent  inhibitors present in the sample that  are removed through the use of irt  so we strongly recommend any irt kit  when dealing with wastewater samples  so i mentioned on the earlier slide that  any irt kit will be recommended so  that's true for any of the r and easy  irt kits and we recommend multiple kits  here because they use a very consistent  chemistry so the rnez power microbiome  the rnez power water and the all prep  power viral dna rna are all suitable for  viral detection and wastewater we have  tested all of them on actual wastewater  samples successfully  and the reason that they are  interchangeable as you can see in this  chart here t