f material that we could  process as a pellet directly into our  kit when we tried to process the  material through the ultrafiltration  membranes or through the mccellulose  esters those methods clogged  and were not able to process more than  10 15 mls  compared to extracting out of 50 mls  when we were doing the pellet system and  as you can see we got much better  detection for that municipal plant when  dealing with the pellet  the other plant that we were dealing  with was a more general plant it  included water flowing over overland  streams had more environmental runoff  and that provided better results with  the filtered material slightly it had  signal in the pellet as well  much more comfortable between all three  methods and was also easily filterable  through all of the methods  so the particular sample used um will  affect  which concentration method is going to  work best in your laboratory um the  important note is that all of our kits  will work well for all concentration  methods  so our recommendations for  doing  rna extraction from wastewater  is to filter your sample  if you filter your sample you should use  the rna z power water kit because that  provides five mil tubes to do processing  of the larger filter if you're going to  concentrate the sample through pelleting  or through ultra filtration then the all  prep power viral dna rna or the rnez  power microbiome kit work well  in our experience of testing different  waste water samples bead beading is not  necessary also not harmful this may vary  depending on your particular sample and  particularly when doing filters bead  beading may help to scrape material off  of those filters  and so we don't  not recommend we don't recommend that  people do not do bead beading but we do  not find that it's necessary likewise  dna's digestion is not necessary when  using these kits  there is a standard protocol for the  iron easy power microbiome kit  and a custom protocol for the all-prep  power viral kit on the kaia cube the  custom protocol can be requested through  our apps lab  and we are working on standardizing and  releasing the all prep power viral also  as a standard  kayak cube process  and that brings me to the end of my  slides and here i'd like to just leave  off with another excerpt from a paper by  dr ahmed  um  concluding that extraction of  lysate using the rnez power microbiome  and kai keep connect platform to obtain  a high quality rna  is highly suitable for wastewater  analysis thank you for your attention  and  i'll hand it over to colin for the  additional pcr portion thank you  thanks dominic now i'm going to tell you  guys how you can use the kai acuity  digital pcr system to detect sars kovi 2  in your wastewater samples  i'd just like to reiterate a few things  that dominic has already said about sars  cov2 and wastewater testing before going  any further  the real advantage of using wastewater  samples to monitor sars kobe 2 is that  within a single sample of wastewater  hundreds thousands and even millions of  people are represented and this allows  researchers to get a much better  snapshot of the community spread of sars  kobe 2 when compared to looking at  individual clinical samples and this  data from wastewater can be used as an  early warning sign for outbreaks and  allows researchers to get a snapshot of  sars cov2varian spread within a single  sample  and they can relate the quantities of  each variant to each other very easily  now digital pcr is particularly well  suited to this  task because unlike qpcr digital pcr is  absolute quantification where no  standard curve is required allowing data  collected from between various sites to  be compared with great certainty and  precision owing to the fact that the  data is absolute in its quantification  additionally because digital pcr  quantitates a little bit differently  from qpcr  the chemistry is a little bit more  robust to  the wastewater samples which are known  to contain  pcr inhibitors  so why is the kai acuity nanoplate  digital pcr system ideal for wastewater  testing  first of all the time to result with the  nanoplate is only two hours which is  much shorter than the five hours it  takes using the conventional digital  droplet pcr system from bio-rad  second  the kai acuity nano plate system is  capable of high multiplexing up to five  plex  meaning that users can detect multiple  sars cov2 variants within a single  reaction well  lastly the kai acuity nanoplate system  is fully integrated  in its workflow and offers users the  flexibility  of throughput and resolution  the plates  are very similar  to qpcr plates in their shape and well  layout and the 24 and 96 well plate  options allow users  the flexibility of throughput and  resolution all at once  i'd like to take a brief moment to point  out the features of the kai acuity  nanoplates and how they differ from the  digital droplet pcr workflow  in the kayaking nanoplate you can see  your results literally in the raw image  of each and every well on your nanoplate  second of all  sealed nanoplates prevent contamination  between wells once your reaction mixes  in a l it's in a closed environment and  it stays there  solid partitions compared to the  droplets have a very reproducible size  and therefore are particularly well  suited for the poisson calculations  that underlie digital pcr which rely on  a distinct and discrete partition volume  because we can image an entire well at  once and not via the flow cytometry  style of digital droplet pcr the readout  is fast  and because our plates are the  standardized format of all  pcr plates  the workflow is very simple and anyone  who's familiar with qpcr will have no  problem jumping in to the kayaking  nanoplate world  of course in order to use the kai acuity  nanoplates you need kai acuity  instruments and here i'd like to talk  about the four instruments that we have  available  we have a single plate instrument calle